{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-269",
  "title": "RFP-SF",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "RFP-SF"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**1. Project Overview**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**RFP #232 - WorkforceCentral and SmallBusiness Central Data Systems**: The City and County of San Francisco, through the Office of Economic and Workforce Development (OEWD), is seeking proposals for services related to the hosting, maintenance, and enhancement of its WorkforceCentral and SmallBusiness Central data systems."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "OEWD has allocated up to $195,000 annually for this project, with a total of $780,000 over four years."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The selected supplier will be responsible for ensuring reliable performance, data security, and system improvements to support OEWD's ability to track outcomes and make informed decisions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The project will be overseen by OEWD's Impact, Policy, and Communications (IPC) Division."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**RFP 2025 - Building & Safety Services**: The City of Lakewood is seeking proposals for Building & Safety Services, including Building Official Services, building administrative support, plan check, building inspection services, and CASp inspections."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**2. Key Requirements and Guidelines (RFP #232)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Proposal Submission**: Proposals for the San Francisco RFP #232 are due by Tuesday, June 3, 2025, and must be submitted online."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Budget**: A completed budget template (Attachment B) in Excel format is a required submission. The budget should include all reasonable and necessary costs associated with the proposed project."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-12",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Contract Terms**: The City's contract terms are provided as a reference (Attachment C) and cover aspects such as definitions, acceptance, authorized users, city data, data breach, deliverables, and contractor responsibilities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-13",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Evaluation**: Proposals will be evaluated based on factors including applicant qualifications, staff assignments, and experience."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Supplier Requirements**: Proposers must be registered as a City Supplier."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**3. Telos Affinity Group (TAG) Capabilities**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-17",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Telos Affinity Group LLC (TAG) is a service-disabled veteran and minority-owned small business."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-18",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "TAG offers a range of services including product strategy, systems architecture, mobile app development, API development, UI/UX design, and branding."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-19",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "TAG's core competencies include Mobile App Development, API Development, Systems Architecture, Product Strategy, and UI/UX Design."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-20",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "TAG emphasizes human-centered design, collaboration, and innovation."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**4. Additional Details (RFP #232)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-23",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The RFP includes questions that applicants must answer in their proposal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-24",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "OEWD's Impact, Policy, and Communications (IPC) Division is responsible for data management and impact measurement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-25",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The selected contractor will be expected to provide services such as system management, data governance, data reporting, and research & evaluation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-26",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The contract is expected to begin in July 2025 and may be extended for up to ten years."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This comprehensive summary should give you a solid overview of the RFPs and TAG's capabilities. Let me know if you have any other questions."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}